### [ ] M8-S4 — EAS production build and internal testing

**Goal:** Build and test the production binary via TestFlight and Google Play Internal Testing before submitting for review.

*EAS Build: Expo's cloud service that compiles your source code into the `.ipa` (iPhone) and `.aab` (Android) files that stores require.*

**Build prompt:**
```
Before building:
  □ Remove Purchases.setLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL.VERBOSE) from src/lib/purchases.ts
  □ Confirm SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are correct (production project)
  □ Confirm RevenueCat public keys are the production keys (not sandbox)

── iOS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Prerequisites: Apple Developer account ($99/year), enrolled in Apple Developer Program.

  eas build --platform ios --profile production

EAS will create provisioning profiles automatically if you say yes to the prompts.
When the build finishes, submit to TestFlight:
  eas submit --platform ios --latest

In App Store Connect → TestFlight → Internal Testers:
  Add yourself. Install the build on your iPhone.

── Android ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Prerequisites: Google Play Developer account ($25 one-time).

  eas build --platform android --profile production
  eas submit --platform android --latest

In Google Play Console → Internal Testing: add yourself as a tester.
Download and install from the Play Store internal testing link.

── Pre-submission checklist (test every item on the real TestFlight build) ──
□ App icon shows correctly on home screen
□ Splash screen appears and hides without a flash
□ Sign up creates a new account
□ Sign in with reviewer credentials works
□ Today screen loads a workout
□ Set logging saves and persists
□ Camera opens, records 10-second video, uploads
□ AI feedback appears within 15 seconds
□ Progress chart shows data
□ History shows past workouts with expand/collapse
□ Paywall loads and shows price
□ Sandbox subscription purchase completes
□ Restore purchases works
